        <p>Want a lawyer to check which claims apply to you?</p>
        <a href="#contact" class="btn btn--primary">Book a Free Consultation</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="mistakes-heading">
      <h2 id="mistakes-heading">Common Mistakes That Cost People Money</h2>
      <p>Most losses come from timing and assumptions rather than from the law itself.</p>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Treating 25% per year as guaranteed.</strong> It is a yardstick the court may adjust.</li>
        <li><strong>Expecting a 50/50 split.</strong> Alimony and property are separate questions.</li>
        <li><strong>Waiting too long.</strong> Past maintenance claims reach back two years for a Muslim wife and one year for children.</li>
        <li><strong>Choosing khul’ without costing it.</strong> There is no iddah maintenance after khul’ (Article 101); see our <a href="/en/khula-divorce-uae/">khula guide</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Moving out without advice.</strong> A Muslim wife’s maintenance lapses if she refuses to live in the marital home without a legitimate excuse (Article 103).</li>
        <li><strong>Filing in ADGM or DIFC.</strong> Neither grants divorces; see <a href="/en/adgm-divorce-abu-dhabi/">ADGM and divorce</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For every right a wife can raise, see
        <a href="/en/wife-rights-after-divorce-uae/">wife’s rights after divorce in the UAE</a>, and
        to have your figures checked, we can connect you with
        <a href="/en/divorce-lawyer-abu-dhabi/">a divorce lawyer in Abu Dhabi</a>.
      </p>
